# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Patient â€” Appointments & Payments â€” public (with internal checks + DB trigger)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Create appointment â€” ðŸ”’ patient (now protected) â€” POST /api/patients/appointments â€” 400 if dept inactive (DB trigger P0001)
# Auth: Bearer {{patientToken}} required (authMiddleware+role patient). patient_id comes from JWT req.user.patient_id, NOT body â€” prevents spoofing. Body: { doctor_id, schedule_id, hospital_id? } hospital optional (uses slot hospital if omitted)
# Uses isSlotExpired() server authority + calculate_appointment_fee() for fee, book_appointment procedure for DB workflow, trg_appointment_department_check still blocks inactive dept.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}

{
  "doctor_id": 1,
  "schedule_id": 1,
  "hospital_id": 1
}

### 4.1b Without JWT â€” expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doctor_id": 1,
  "schedule_id": 1
}

### 4.2 List own appointments â€” public â€” GET /api/patients/:patientId/appointments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/1/appointments

### 4.3 Cancel pending â€” public â€” DELETE /api/patients/appointments/:id
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/appointments/1

### 4.4 Make payment â€” public â€” POST /api/patients/payments â€” fires trg_payment_success + trg_appointment_status_notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patient_id": 1,
  "appointment_id": 1,
  "payment_method": "bkash"
}

